GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
One photo plane, front face drawn TRUE (undistorted rectangle ~4×4 world units in XY, portrait-aspect acceptable at 4×4.5), with depth receding along a single diagonal (+Z) as a thin extruded edge ~0.08 deep, matching the slight tilt in the source. The photo content is a graffiti mural: girl with black bob hair in a yellow hoodie holding white signs with red lettering ('GIVE PEACE A CHANCE', 'FOR ALL KIDS'), red hearts, pink/red paint on grey concrete — a simplified stylized recreation suffices (flat colored shapes: yellow torso, pink face, red text scribbles on grey background). Grid lines black, ~0.02 thick, raised slightly above the photo surface. Regular N×N grid: lines at i/N for i=0..N. Offset grid: lines at (i-0.5)/N, clipping to the photo so edge windows are partial (half-width at the borders, quarter-size at corners). Tiles separated by thin white gaps (~0.03 units) to mimic the cut-tile look of the source. Label text centered below the plane. Clicked tile: highlight fill #ff8800 at 0.25 opacity with orange border; token dots dark blue #1a3366 arranged 4×4 within the tile; attention lines semi-transparent blue between all token pairs.

